            <div xml:id="d83">

                <pb facs="0185" n="155" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v5/pg155"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">No. 57.</note>
                <head>Mr. Campbell to the Secretary of State.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1872-01-19"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 19, 1872.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: * * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I can say from my own knowledge that after the discovery of gold on Fraser River
                    in 1858, the canal de Haro was the *ordinary channel of communication between
                    Victoria and British Columbia, and doubtless now is, and ever will be.<seg
                        type="margin">[71]</seg><seg type="margin">The Haro channel the usual
                        channel.</seg></p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>ARCHIBALD CAMPBELL, <hi rendition="#italic">Late United States Boundary
                            Commissioner.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
